# Test: parser handles [fn [let x y] body] params directly, no macro needed.
# [fn [let x y] body] is parsed as Expr::Fn by the parser — it never reaches the fn macro.
# syntax.llt is a no-op stub; the include does nothing. This is a regression test
# for the parser's direct Fn node construction, not for macro expansion.
[include %libdir "syntax.llt"]
[result: [[fn [let x y] [+ x y]] 3 4]]
=== out
Int(7)
